{
 "language": "en",
 "model": "small.en",
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 35.7,
   "end": 38.3,
   "text": "Many of the materials we work with in our labs",
   "zh": "我们在实验室里使用的许多物质"
  },
  {
   "start": 38.3,
   "end": 41.62,
   "text": "give off fumes, mists, vapors, particulates,",
   "zh": "会散发出烟气、雾、蒸气、颗粒物"
  },
  {
   "start": 41.62,
   "end": 43.86,
   "text": "or aerosols that are hazardous.",
   "zh": "或气溶胶，这些都是有害的。"
  },
  {
   "start": 43.86,
   "end": 46.1,
   "text": "To minimize exposure to these materials,",
   "zh": "为了尽量减少对这些物质的接触，"
  },
  {
   "start": 46.1,
   "end": 48.98,
   "text": "we need to take special precautions.",
   "zh": "我们需要采取特别的预防措施。"
  },
  {
   "start": 48.98,
   "end": 51.82,
   "text": "Often, this means working within a hood.",
   "zh": "这通常意味着要在通风柜内操作。"
  },
  {
   "start": 53.58,
   "end": 55.9,
   "text": "We can get an idea of how to work safely with hoods",
   "zh": "要了解如何安全地使用通风柜，"
  },
  {
   "start": 55.9,
   "end": 58.74,
   "text": "by looking at one of the most frequently used types,",
   "zh": "我们可以看看最常用的类型之一，"
  },
  {
   "start": 58.74,
   "end": 74.08,
   "text": "the chemical exhaust hood.",
   "zh": "化学排风通风柜。"
  },
  {
   "start": 74.08,
   "end": 76.8,
   "text": "Exhaust hoods protect us by preventing contaminants",
   "zh": "排风通风柜保护我们的方式，是防止柜内的污染物"
  },
  {
   "start": 76.8,
   "end": 80.08,
   "text": "within the hood from entering our breathing zone.",
   "zh": "进入我们的呼吸区。"
  },
  {
   "start": 80.08,
   "end": 82.36,
   "text": "A protective barrier is created by air",
   "zh": "被吸入并流经通风柜的空气"
  },
  {
   "start": 82.36,
   "end": 85.32,
   "text": "that's pulled into and through the hood.",
   "zh": "形成了一道保护屏障。"
  },
  {
   "start": 85.32,
   "end": 88.8,
   "text": "This inward airflow helps keep hazardous fumes and vapors",
   "zh": "这种向内的气流有助于阻止有害烟气和蒸气"
  },
  {
   "start": 88.8,
   "end": 93.12,
   "text": "from escaping and reaching anyone outside the hood.",
   "zh": "逸出，到达通风柜外的任何人。"
  },
  {
   "start": 93.12,
   "end": 95.4,
   "text": "Contaminants that are captured within the airflow",
   "zh": "被气流捕获的污染物"
  },
  {
   "start": 95.4,
   "end": 97.88,
   "text": "are filtered, diluted, and exhausted",
   "zh": "经过过滤、稀释，然后通过"
  },
  {
   "start": 97.88,
   "end": 101.35,
   "text": "through the hood's duct system.",
   "zh": "通风柜的风管系统排出。"
  },
  {
   "start": 101.35,
   "end": 103.79,
   "text": "This air is then sent outside the building,",
   "zh": "这些空气随后被排到建筑物外，"
  },
  {
   "start": 103.79,
   "end": 105.67,
   "text": "where the contaminants are further diluted",
   "zh": "污染物在那里进一步被稀释"
  },
  {
   "start": 105.67,
   "end": 108.78,
   "text": "into the atmosphere.",
   "zh": "到大气中。"
  },
  {
   "start": 108.78,
   "end": 110.58,
   "text": "Hoods also protect the operator",
   "zh": "通风柜还能保护操作者"
  },
  {
   "start": 110.58,
   "end": 112.62,
   "text": "from other physical threats.",
   "zh": "免受其他物理威胁。"
  },
  {
   "start": 112.62,
   "end": 114.98,
   "text": "The sash provides protection from hazards",
   "zh": "柜门能防护诸如"
  },
  {
   "start": 114.98,
   "end": 117.14,
   "text": "like chemical splashes and sprays,",
   "zh": "化学品飞溅和喷溅之类的危害，"
  },
  {
   "start": 117.14,
   "end": 119.98,
   "text": "as well as fires and minor explosions.",
   "zh": "以及火灾和小型爆炸。"
  },
  {
   "start": 119.98,
   "end": 122.06,
   "text": "Generally, you want to pull the sash down",
   "zh": "一般来说，你要把柜门尽量"
  },
  {
   "start": 122.06,
   "end": 123.34,
   "text": "as far as possible,",
   "zh": "往下拉，"
  },
  {
   "start": 123.34,
   "end": 124.7,
   "text": "while keeping it at a level",
   "zh": "同时让它保持在一个"
  },
  {
   "start": 124.7,
   "end": 128.5,
   "text": "that allows you to work comfortably.",
   "zh": "能让你舒适操作的高度。"
  },
  {
   "start": 128.5,
   "end": 130.5,
   "text": "Many hood manufacturers have determined",
   "zh": "许多通风柜制造商已经确定了"
  },
  {
   "start": 130.5,
   "end": 132.7,
   "text": "the levels at which the sashes in their hoods",
   "zh": "其通风柜的柜门"
  },
  {
   "start": 132.7,
   "end": 135.18,
   "text": "should be placed for maximum protection,",
   "zh": "应处于什么高度才能提供最大保护，"
  },
  {
   "start": 135.18,
   "end": 137.42,
   "text": "so you'll want to follow their recommendations",
   "zh": "所以你要尽可能"
  },
  {
   "start": 137.42,
   "end": 141.18,
   "text": "if at all possible.",
   "zh": "遵循他们的建议。"
  },
  {
   "start": 141.18,
   "end": 142.62,
   "text": "When working within a hood,",
   "zh": "在通风柜内操作时，"
  },
  {
   "start": 142.62,
   "end": 145.38,
   "text": "don't forget to wear the personal protective equipment",
   "zh": "别忘了穿戴个人防护装备，"
  },
  {
   "start": 145.38,
   "end": 148.26,
   "text": "that the materials you're using call for.",
   "zh": "按照你所用物质的要求。"
  },
  {
   "start": 148.26,
   "end": 150.06,
   "text": "Even with a hood's protection,",
   "zh": "即使有通风柜的保护，"
  },
  {
   "start": 150.06,
   "end": 152.58,
   "text": "you need to wear at least the safety eyewear,",
   "zh": "你至少也需要佩戴平常使用的安全护目镜，"
  },
  {
   "start": 152.58,
   "end": 157.1,
   "text": "lab coat, and gloves that you normally use.",
   "zh": "穿实验服、戴手套。"
  },
  {
   "start": 157.1,
   "end": 160.42,
   "text": "You should also read the substance's safety data sheets.",
   "zh": "你还应该阅读该物质的安全技术说明书。"
  },
  {
   "start": 160.42,
   "end": 162.78,
   "text": "These will tell you each substance's ingredients,",
   "zh": "它们会告诉你每种物质的成分、"
  },
  {
   "start": 162.78,
   "end": 165.62,
   "text": "properties, and hazards.",
   "zh": "性质和危害。"
  },
  {
   "start": 165.62,
   "end": 167.38,
   "text": "And if the substances you're working with",
   "zh": "如果你所使用的物质"
  },
  {
   "start": 167.38,
   "end": 169.22,
   "text": "require additional protection,",
   "zh": "需要额外的防护，"
  },
  {
   "start": 169.22,
   "end": 184.66,
   "text": "you should use it as well.",
   "zh": "你也应该采用。"
  },
  {
   "start": 184.66,
   "end": 186.74,
   "text": "To ensure that it's operating safely,",
   "zh": "为确保安全运行，"
  },
  {
   "start": 186.74,
   "end": 188.62,
   "text": "each lab hood is thoroughly tested",
   "zh": "每台实验室通风柜都要进行全面测试："
  },
  {
   "start": 188.62,
   "end": 190.06,
   "text": "when it's first installed,",
   "zh": "在首次安装时，"
  },
  {
   "start": 190.06,
   "end": 192.82,
   "text": "whenever there's a change in the ventilation system",
   "zh": "在通风系统发生任何变化时，"
  },
  {
   "start": 192.82,
   "end": 195.9,
   "text": "and on a regular basis thereafter.",
   "zh": "以及此后定期进行。"
  },
  {
   "start": 195.9,
   "end": 198.14,
   "text": "There are specific steps that need to be taken",
   "zh": "要确定一台通风柜是否按应有的方式运行，"
  },
  {
   "start": 198.14,
   "end": 202.74,
   "text": "to determine if a hood is operating the way it should.",
   "zh": "需要采取一些特定的步骤。"
  },
  {
   "start": 202.74,
   "end": 206.46,
   "text": "First, the air circulation around the hood should be checked.",
   "zh": "首先，要检查通风柜周围的空气流动。"
  },
  {
   "start": 206.46,
   "end": 209.14,
   "text": "Your supervisor or a qualified engineer",
   "zh": "你的主管或合格的工程师"
  },
  {
   "start": 209.14,
   "end": 210.42,
   "text": "will measure the flow of air",
   "zh": "会测量通风柜前方"
  },
  {
   "start": 210.42,
   "end": 212.78,
   "text": "six inches in front of the hood.",
   "zh": "六英寸处的气流。"
  },
  {
   "start": 212.78,
   "end": 216.02,
   "text": "This cross-draft should be monitored carefully.",
   "zh": "这种横向气流应受到仔细监测。"
  },
  {
   "start": 216.02,
   "end": 218.5,
   "text": "Drafts greater than 20 linear feet per minute",
   "zh": "大于每分钟 20 线性英尺的横向气流"
  },
  {
   "start": 218.5,
   "end": 221.26,
   "text": "will adversely affect the performance of the hood.",
   "zh": "会对通风柜的性能产生不利影响。"
  },
  {
   "start": 222.98,
   "end": 225.34,
   "text": "Next, a smoke tube should be used",
   "zh": "接下来，应该使用发烟管"
  },
  {
   "start": 225.34,
   "end": 226.94,
   "text": "to make sure that the air is flowing",
   "zh": "来确认通风柜内的空气"
  },
  {
   "start": 226.94,
   "end": 229.22,
   "text": "as it should inside the hood.",
   "zh": "按应有的方式流动。"
  },
  {
   "start": 229.22,
   "end": 231.42,
   "text": "If the smoke heads for the ventilation ducts,",
   "zh": "如果烟朝着通风管道流去，"
  },
  {
   "start": 231.42,
   "end": 235.64,
   "text": "then the hood is operating correctly.",
   "zh": "那么通风柜就运行正常。"
  },
  {
   "start": 235.64,
   "end": 237.4,
   "text": "It's then time to open the sash",
   "zh": "然后就该打开柜门，"
  },
  {
   "start": 237.4,
   "end": 238.56,
   "text": "and measure the rate of air",
   "zh": "测量通过通风柜开口面的"
  },
  {
   "start": 238.56,
   "end": 240.76,
   "text": "coming through the face of the hood.",
   "zh": "空气流速。"
  },
  {
   "start": 240.76,
   "end": 246.19,
   "text": "This measurement is known as the hood's face velocity.",
   "zh": "这个测量值就叫做通风柜的面风速。"
  },
  {
   "start": 246.19,
   "end": 248.59,
   "text": "An accurate measurement of the face velocity",
   "zh": "准确地测量面风速"
  },
  {
   "start": 248.59,
   "end": 250.23,
   "text": "is very important,",
   "zh": "非常重要，"
  },
  {
   "start": 250.23,
   "end": 252.55,
   "text": "so a precision instrument like an anemometer",
   "zh": "所以应该使用风速计"
  },
  {
   "start": 252.55,
   "end": 254.43,
   "text": "or a velometer should be used.",
   "zh": "或速度计这样的精密仪器。"
  },
  {
   "start": 255.47,
   "end": 257.99,
   "text": "Never try to use something like sheets of tissue paper",
   "zh": "绝不要尝试用纸巾之类的东西"
  },
  {
   "start": 257.99,
   "end": 260.55,
   "text": "to give you an indication of face velocity.",
   "zh": "来判断面风速。"
  },
  {
   "start": 260.55,
   "end": 265.92,
   "text": "They will only show you whether the hood is on or off.",
   "zh": "它们只能告诉你通风柜是开着还是关着。"
  },
  {
   "start": 265.92,
   "end": 267.84,
   "text": "When measuring face velocity,",
   "zh": "测量面风速时，"
  },
  {
   "start": 267.84,
   "end": 269.4,
   "text": "the sash should be adjusted",
   "zh": "应该把柜门调整到"
  },
  {
   "start": 269.4,
   "end": 271.28,
   "text": "as if you were about to begin work.",
   "zh": "就像你要开始操作时那样。"
  },
  {
   "start": 272.28,
   "end": 274.4,
   "text": "Your supervisor will divide the hood face",
   "zh": "你的主管会把通风柜开口面"
  },
  {
   "start": 274.4,
   "end": 275.6,
   "text": "into a grid pattern",
   "zh": "划分成网格，"
  },
  {
   "start": 275.6,
   "end": 279.0,
   "text": "and measure the velocity of the air in each section.",
   "zh": "并测量每个网格内的空气流速。"
  },
  {
   "start": 279.0,
   "end": 281.28,
   "text": "Values at specific points may vary",
   "zh": "特定点的数值可以有"
  },
  {
   "start": 281.28,
   "end": 283.44,
   "text": "by plus or minus 25%",
   "zh": "正负 25% 的偏差，"
  },
  {
   "start": 283.44,
   "end": 286.48,
   "text": "without compromising the safety of the hood's operation.",
   "zh": "而不影响通风柜运行的安全性。"
  },
  {
   "start": 288.04,
   "end": 289.6,
   "text": "But no measurement should be below",
   "zh": "但任何一个测量值都不应低于"
  },
  {
   "start": 289.6,
   "end": 291.68,
   "text": "60 linear feet per minute.",
   "zh": "每分钟 60 线性英尺。"
  },
  {
   "start": 291.68,
   "end": 293.92,
   "text": "If your test shows a lower speed,",
   "zh": "如果你的测试显示速度更低，"
  },
  {
   "start": 293.92,
   "end": 295.24,
   "text": "the airflow should be adjusted",
   "zh": "就应该先调整气流，"
  },
  {
   "start": 295.24,
   "end": 297.04,
   "text": "before the hood is used again.",
   "zh": "然后才能再次使用通风柜。"
  },
  {
   "start": 298.68,
   "end": 300.52,
   "text": "Your supervisor will also compare",
   "zh": "你的主管还会比较"
  },
  {
   "start": 300.6,
   "end": 303.36,
   "text": "the face velocity of the air coming through the hood",
   "zh": "通过通风柜的空气面风速"
  },
  {
   "start": 303.36,
   "end": 305.32,
   "text": "with the speed of the cross draft",
   "zh": "与横向气流的速度，"
  },
  {
   "start": 305.32,
   "end": 306.88,
   "text": "to make sure that the cross draft",
   "zh": "以确保横向气流"
  },
  {
   "start": 306.88,
   "end": 310.52,
   "text": "is never greater than 20% of the face velocity.",
   "zh": "绝不大于面风速的 20%。"
  },
  {
   "start": 310.52,
   "end": 311.68,
   "text": "If this is a problem,",
   "zh": "如果这方面有问题，"
  },
  {
   "start": 311.68,
   "end": 314.04,
   "text": "the interior hood baffle will be adjusted",
   "zh": "就会调整通风柜内部的导流板，"
  },
  {
   "start": 314.04,
   "end": 315.24,
   "text": "or if necessary,",
   "zh": "或者在必要时，"
  },
  {
   "start": 315.24,
   "end": 317.2,
   "text": "the ventilation of the laboratory itself",
   "zh": "可能需要改变"
  },
  {
   "start": 317.2,
   "end": 318.6,
   "text": "may need to be altered.",
   "zh": "实验室本身的通风。"
  },
  {
   "start": 320.2,
   "end": 322.24,
   "text": "In general, hoods will bring in air",
   "zh": "一般来说，通风柜吸入空气的"
  },
  {
   "start": 322.24,
   "end": 323.48,
   "text": "at a face velocity",
   "zh": "面风速"
  },
  {
   "start": 323.48,
   "end": 326.52,
   "text": "of about 80 to 100 linear feet per minute,",
   "zh": "约为每分钟 80 到 100 线性英尺，"
  },
  {
   "start": 326.52,
   "end": 328.8,
   "text": "but you may need to use a higher velocity",
   "zh": "但对于你所做的某些工作，"
  },
  {
   "start": 328.8,
   "end": 331.2,
   "text": "for some of the work that you do.",
   "zh": "可能需要使用更高的风速。"
  },
  {
   "start": 331.2,
   "end": 334.36,
   "text": "A velocity of about 125 linear feet per minute",
   "zh": "某些操作可能需要"
  },
  {
   "start": 334.36,
   "end": 337.32,
   "text": "may be required for some procedures.",
   "zh": "约每分钟 125 线性英尺的风速。"
  },
  {
   "start": 337.32,
   "end": 338.52,
   "text": "Be careful, though.",
   "zh": "不过要小心。"
  },
  {
   "start": 338.52,
   "end": 340.72,
   "text": "Higher velocities can create turbulence",
   "zh": "较高的风速会产生湍流，"
  },
  {
   "start": 340.72,
   "end": 342.0,
   "text": "both inside a hood",
   "zh": "既在通风柜内部，"
  },
  {
   "start": 342.0,
   "end": 344.88,
   "text": "and at the front of the hood face.",
   "zh": "也在通风柜开口面的前方。"
  },
  {
   "start": 344.88,
   "end": 346.64,
   "text": "This can cause vapors within the hood",
   "zh": "这会导致通风柜内的蒸气"
  },
  {
   "start": 346.64,
   "end": 348.84,
   "text": "to spill out into the laboratory,",
   "zh": "溢出到实验室中，"
  },
  {
   "start": 348.84,
   "end": 351.68,
   "text": "putting you and your coworkers at risk.",
   "zh": "使你和你的同事处于危险之中。"
  },
  {
   "start": 351.68,
   "end": 353.52,
   "text": "In general, face velocity",
   "zh": "一般来说，面风速"
  },
  {
   "start": 353.52,
   "end": 357.52,
   "text": "should not exceed 150 linear feet per minute.",
   "zh": "不应超过每分钟 150 线性英尺。"
  },
  {
   "start": 357.52,
   "end": 358.96,
   "text": "And remember, you should have",
   "zh": "还要记住，你应该让人"
  },
  {
   "start": 358.96,
   "end": 360.6,
   "text": "the face velocity of your hoods",
   "zh": "对你的通风柜的面风速"
  },
  {
   "start": 360.6,
   "end": 365.56,
   "text": "measured regularly once a year at minimum.",
   "zh": "定期进行测量，至少每年一次。"
  },
  {
   "start": 365.56,
   "end": 367.8,
   "text": "Once it's determined that the air velocities",
   "zh": "一旦确定通风柜内部及周围的"
  },
  {
   "start": 367.8,
   "end": 368.8,
   "text": "in and around the hood",
   "zh": "空气流速"
  },
  {
   "start": 368.8,
   "end": 370.4,
   "text": "are within accepted ranges,",
   "zh": "都在可接受的范围内，"
  },
  {
   "start": 370.4,
   "end": 371.84,
   "text": "it's important to make sure the hood",
   "zh": "就要确保通风柜内"
  },
  {
   "start": 371.84,
   "end": 374.64,
   "text": "is relatively free of air turbulence.",
   "zh": "相对没有空气湍流，这一点很重要。"
  },
  {
   "start": 374.64,
   "end": 375.84,
   "text": "Turbulence can be checked",
   "zh": "湍流可以通过"
  },
  {
   "start": 375.84,
   "end": 378.84,
   "text": "by observing smoke patterns within the hood.",
   "zh": "观察通风柜内的烟雾形态来检查。"
  },
  {
   "start": 378.84,
   "end": 380.4,
   "text": "If there's excessive turbulence",
   "zh": "如果湍流过大，"
  },
  {
   "start": 380.4,
   "end": 382.56,
   "text": "or if the hood fails to capture the smoke,",
   "zh": "或者通风柜未能捕获烟雾，"
  },
  {
   "start": 382.56,
   "end": 384.8,
   "text": "adjustments will be required.",
   "zh": "就需要进行调整。"
  },
  {
   "start": 384.8,
   "end": 386.6,
   "text": "The engineer who is working on the hood",
   "zh": "负责这台通风柜的工程师"
  },
  {
   "start": 386.6,
   "end": 388.64,
   "text": "will consider changing a number of things,",
   "zh": "会考虑改变若干方面，"
  },
  {
   "start": 388.64,
   "end": 392.24,
   "text": "such as the location of equipment within the hood,",
   "zh": "比如设备在通风柜内的位置、"
  },
  {
   "start": 392.24,
   "end": 394.16,
   "text": "the hood's face velocity,",
   "zh": "通风柜的面风速、"
  },
  {
   "start": 394.16,
   "end": 396.68,
   "text": "the location of air input ports,",
   "zh": "进风口的位置、"
  },
  {
   "start": 396.68,
   "end": 398.76,
   "text": "the physical location of the hood,",
   "zh": "通风柜的实际安放位置，"
  },
  {
   "start": 398.76,
   "end": 399.88,
   "text": "and the volume of air",
   "zh": "以及进入通风柜的"
  },
  {
   "start": 399.88,
   "end": 403.39,
   "text": "being brought into the hood.",
   "zh": "空气量。"
  },
  {
   "start": 403.39,
   "end": 404.43,
   "text": "As you can see,",
   "zh": "如你所见，"
  },
  {
   "start": 404.43,
   "end": 406.51,
   "text": "there is a lot that goes into making sure",
   "zh": "要确保一台通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 406.51,
   "end": 408.47,
   "text": "that a hood is functioning properly.",
   "zh": "正常运行，涉及很多方面。"
  },
  {
   "start": 408.47,
   "end": 410.11,
   "text": "If you suspect that your hood",
   "zh": "如果你怀疑你的通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 410.11,
   "end": 411.75,
   "text": "isn't performing as it should,",
   "zh": "性能不达标，"
  },
  {
   "start": 411.75,
   "end": 413.03,
   "text": "talk to your supervisor",
   "zh": "就和你的主管谈一谈，"
  },
  {
   "start": 413.03,
   "end": 429.47,
   "text": "to determine if a reevaluation is needed.",
   "zh": "以确定是否需要重新评估。"
  },
  {
   "start": 429.47,
   "end": 431.47,
   "text": "Having a lab hood set up correctly",
   "zh": "把实验室通风柜设置正确"
  },
  {
   "start": 431.47,
   "end": 433.43,
   "text": "is just half the battle.",
   "zh": "只是成功了一半。"
  },
  {
   "start": 433.43,
   "end": 435.11,
   "text": "In order for hoods to be effective,",
   "zh": "要让通风柜发挥作用，"
  },
  {
   "start": 435.11,
   "end": 438.07,
   "text": "we've also got to use them correctly.",
   "zh": "我们还必须正确地使用它们。"
  },
  {
   "start": 438.07,
   "end": 439.91,
   "text": "This means doing everything we can",
   "zh": "这意味着要尽一切努力"
  },
  {
   "start": 439.91,
   "end": 442.99,
   "text": "to maintain proper airflow within the hood.",
   "zh": "保持通风柜内的正常气流。"
  },
  {
   "start": 444.15,
   "end": 445.03,
   "text": "To begin with,",
   "zh": "首先，"
  },
  {
   "start": 445.03,
   "end": 446.79,
   "text": "the work you do should be performed",
   "zh": "你的操作应该在"
  },
  {
   "start": 446.79,
   "end": 449.59,
   "text": "at least six inches inside the hood.",
   "zh": "通风柜内至少六英寸处进行。"
  },
  {
   "start": 449.59,
   "end": 451.59,
   "text": "This enables the airflow within the hood",
   "zh": "这样通风柜内的气流就能"
  },
  {
   "start": 451.59,
   "end": 453.47,
   "text": "to capture any dangerous vapors",
   "zh": "捕获开口面附近的"
  },
  {
   "start": 453.47,
   "end": 455.27,
   "text": "and particles near the face",
   "zh": "任何危险蒸气和颗粒，"
  },
  {
   "start": 455.27,
   "end": 456.87,
   "text": "and prevent them from escaping",
   "zh": "并防止它们逸出"
  },
  {
   "start": 456.87,
   "end": 458.39,
   "text": "into your breathing zone.",
   "zh": "进入你的呼吸区。"
  },
  {
   "start": 459.39,
   "end": 461.19,
   "text": "Since large pieces of equipment",
   "zh": "由于大型设备，"
  },
  {
   "start": 461.19,
   "end": 462.39,
   "text": "such as orbital shakers",
   "zh": "比如回旋式摇床，"
  },
  {
   "start": 462.39,
   "end": 464.39,
   "text": "can obstruct the airflow within a hood,",
   "zh": "会阻碍通风柜内的气流，"
  },
  {
   "start": 464.39,
   "end": 465.51,
   "text": "they should be elevated",
   "zh": "应该把它们垫高，"
  },
  {
   "start": 465.51,
   "end": 467.87,
   "text": "to allow air to pass under them.",
   "zh": "让空气能从下面流过。"
  },
  {
   "start": 469.15,
   "end": 471.59,
   "text": "Never use hoods as storage cabinets.",
   "zh": "绝不要把通风柜当作储物柜使用。"
  },
  {
   "start": 471.59,
   "end": 473.87,
   "text": "Overloading a hood restricts its airflow",
   "zh": "通风柜里放的东西过多会限制气流，"
  },
  {
   "start": 473.87,
   "end": 475.91,
   "text": "and can result in the dangerous buildup",
   "zh": "并可能导致有害蒸气"
  },
  {
   "start": 475.91,
   "end": 477.99,
   "text": "of hazardous vapors.",
   "zh": "危险地积聚。"
  },
  {
   "start": 477.99,
   "end": 481.47,
   "text": "Additionally, chemicals that are stored",
   "zh": "此外，储存在"
  },
  {
   "start": 481.47,
   "end": 483.27,
   "text": "inside a hood can make an incident",
   "zh": "通风柜内的化学品会使溅洒"
  },
  {
   "start": 483.27,
   "end": 486.47,
   "text": "such as a spill or fire even worse.",
   "zh": "或火灾之类的事故变得更糟。"
  },
  {
   "start": 486.47,
   "end": 489.07,
   "text": "So if you're not actively working with a chemical,",
   "zh": "所以如果你当前没有在使用某种化学品，"
  },
  {
   "start": 489.19,
   "end": 491.71,
   "text": "put it in its normal storage space.",
   "zh": "就把它放回正常的储存位置。"
  },
  {
   "start": 492.71,
   "end": 494.63,
   "text": "You should also keep the sash closed",
   "zh": "不在通风柜里操作时，"
  },
  {
   "start": 494.63,
   "end": 495.75,
   "text": "as much as possible",
   "zh": "你还应该尽量"
  },
  {
   "start": 495.75,
   "end": 497.59,
   "text": "when you're not working in your hood.",
   "zh": "保持柜门关闭。"
  },
  {
   "start": 497.59,
   "end": 498.55,
   "text": "Remember to consult",
   "zh": "记得参考"
  },
  {
   "start": 498.55,
   "end": 500.71,
   "text": "the manufacturer's recommendations.",
   "zh": "制造商的建议。"
  },
  {
   "start": 501.67,
   "end": 504.39,
   "text": "And pay attention to the hood's own air monitors.",
   "zh": "并留意通风柜自带的气流监测器。"
  },
  {
   "start": 504.39,
   "end": 505.79,
   "text": "They'll warn you when the airflow",
   "zh": "当通过通风柜的气流"
  },
  {
   "start": 505.79,
   "end": 507.27,
   "text": "through the hood isn't strong enough",
   "zh": "不够强、"
  },
  {
   "start": 507.27,
   "end": 511.43,
   "text": "to contain the hazards within it.",
   "zh": "不足以把危害控制在柜内时，它们会向你发出警告。"
  },
  {
   "start": 511.43,
   "end": 512.79,
   "text": "It's important to be careful",
   "zh": "在通风柜前，"
  },
  {
   "start": 512.79,
   "end": 514.19,
   "text": "about how you move",
   "zh": "你如何移动"
  },
  {
   "start": 514.19,
   "end": 516.75,
   "text": "when you're in front of a hood as well.",
   "zh": "也要多加小心，这很重要。"
  },
  {
   "start": 516.75,
   "end": 518.11,
   "text": "Even face velocities",
   "zh": "即使是每分钟"
  },
  {
   "start": 518.11,
   "end": 519.79,
   "text": "of 100 linear feet per minute",
   "zh": "100 线性英尺的面风速，"
  },
  {
   "start": 519.99,
   "end": 521.35,
   "text": "can easily be disrupted",
   "zh": "也很容易被扰乱，"
  },
  {
   "start": 521.35,
   "end": 522.95,
   "text": "by rapidly removing your arms",
   "zh": "只要你把手臂快速地"
  },
  {
   "start": 522.95,
   "end": 524.87,
   "text": "from inside a hood.",
   "zh": "从通风柜内抽出来。"
  },
  {
   "start": 524.87,
   "end": 526.95,
   "text": "Even just walking by the hood face",
   "zh": "甚至只是从通风柜开口面前走过，"
  },
  {
   "start": 526.95,
   "end": 528.91,
   "text": "can cause problems.",
   "zh": "也可能造成问题。"
  },
  {
   "start": 528.91,
   "end": 530.19,
   "text": "So you need to be careful",
   "zh": "所以你需要小心"
  },
  {
   "start": 530.19,
   "end": 532.11,
   "text": "of any physical movements you make",
   "zh": "自己做出的任何身体动作，"
  },
  {
   "start": 532.11,
   "end": 534.19,
   "text": "that might alter a hood's airflow.",
   "zh": "以免改变通风柜的气流。"
  },
  {
   "start": 535.11,
   "end": 536.87,
   "text": "After all, most hoods aren't even",
   "zh": "毕竟，大多数通风柜的功率"
  },
  {
   "start": 536.87,
   "end": 538.67,
   "text": "as powerful as a vacuum cleaner.",
   "zh": "甚至还不如一台吸尘器。"
  },
  {
   "start": 539.67,
   "end": 541.35,
   "text": "Another thing you need to guard against",
   "zh": "你还需要防止的另一件事，"
  },
  {
   "start": 541.35,
   "end": 543.71,
   "text": "is solid objects such as papers",
   "zh": "是纸张之类的固体物件"
  },
  {
   "start": 543.71,
   "end": 545.75,
   "text": "entering the exhaust ducts of a hood.",
   "zh": "进入通风柜的排风管道。"
  },
  {
   "start": 545.75,
   "end": 547.19,
   "text": "If they lodge in the ducts",
   "zh": "如果它们卡在管道"
  },
  {
   "start": 547.19,
   "end": 548.51,
   "text": "or the hood's fans,",
   "zh": "或通风柜的风机里，"
  },
  {
   "start": 548.51,
   "end": 550.31,
   "text": "it will significantly degrade",
   "zh": "就会大大降低"
  },
  {
   "start": 550.31,
   "end": 552.03,
   "text": "the effectiveness of the hood.",
   "zh": "通风柜的效能。"
  },
  {
   "start": 553.55,
   "end": 555.39,
   "text": "And never place your head",
   "zh": "绝不要把头"
  },
  {
   "start": 555.39,
   "end": 557.27,
   "text": "inside an exhaust hood.",
   "zh": "伸进排风通风柜里。"
  },
  {
   "start": 557.27,
   "end": 559.63,
   "text": "Not only will it disrupt the airflow,",
   "zh": "这不仅会扰乱气流，"
  },
  {
   "start": 559.63,
   "end": 560.59,
   "text": "you could be overcome",
   "zh": "你还可能被"
  },
  {
   "start": 560.59,
   "end": 563.11,
   "text": "by hazardous fumes or vapors.",
   "zh": "有害烟气或蒸气熏倒。"
  },
  {
   "start": 563.11,
   "end": 564.63,
   "text": "If you need to make adjustments",
   "zh": "如果你需要在通风柜内"
  },
  {
   "start": 564.63,
   "end": 565.75,
   "text": "inside the hood,",
   "zh": "进行调整，"
  },
  {
   "start": 565.75,
   "end": 581.44,
   "text": "talk to your supervisor.",
   "zh": "就和你的主管谈一谈。"
  },
  {
   "start": 581.44,
   "end": 582.92,
   "text": "Most of the hoods we work with",
   "zh": "我们使用的大多数通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 582.92,
   "end": 584.0,
   "text": "are designed to keep us",
   "zh": "都是为了防止我们"
  },
  {
   "start": 584.0,
   "end": 585.68,
   "text": "from breathing in hazardous fumes",
   "zh": "吸入有害烟气"
  },
  {
   "start": 585.68,
   "end": 586.76,
   "text": "and vapors.",
   "zh": "和蒸气而设计的。"
  },
  {
   "start": 586.76,
   "end": 588.32,
   "text": "However, there are also hoods",
   "zh": "不过，也有一些通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 588.32,
   "end": 589.44,
   "text": "that are built to take care",
   "zh": "是专门用来处理"
  },
  {
   "start": 589.44,
   "end": 591.48,
   "text": "of hazardous particles.",
   "zh": "有害颗粒物的。"
  },
  {
   "start": 591.48,
   "end": 593.4,
   "text": "Biohazard hoods, for example,",
   "zh": "例如生物安全柜，"
  },
  {
   "start": 593.4,
   "end": 594.6,
   "text": "are designed to capture",
   "zh": "就是为了捕获"
  },
  {
   "start": 594.6,
   "end": 597.36,
   "text": "toxic and infectious particulates.",
   "zh": "有毒和感染性颗粒物而设计的。"
  },
  {
   "start": 597.36,
   "end": 599.28,
   "text": "These types of hoods are most often",
   "zh": "这类安全柜最常用于"
  },
  {
   "start": 599.28,
   "end": 600.64,
   "text": "used with work involving",
   "zh": "涉及临床样本"
  },
  {
   "start": 600.64,
   "end": 603.08,
   "text": "clinical specimens or body fluids.",
   "zh": "或体液的工作。"
  },
  {
   "start": 604.6,
   "end": 605.72,
   "text": "The major difference",
   "zh": "这些颗粒物安全柜的"
  },
  {
   "start": 605.72,
   "end": 607.12,
   "text": "in these particulate cabinets",
   "zh": "主要区别"
  },
  {
   "start": 607.12,
   "end": 608.88,
   "text": "is their filtering systems.",
   "zh": "在于它们的过滤系统。"
  },
  {
   "start": 608.88,
   "end": 610.48,
   "text": "Not only are these systems able",
   "zh": "这些系统不仅能够"
  },
  {
   "start": 610.48,
   "end": 612.24,
   "text": "to capture very fine particles",
   "zh": "捕获非常细小的颗粒"
  },
  {
   "start": 612.24,
   "end": 613.08,
   "text": "and aerosols,",
   "zh": "和气溶胶，"
  },
  {
   "start": 613.08,
   "end": 614.64,
   "text": "but they don't evacuate",
   "zh": "而且不会把这些污染物"
  },
  {
   "start": 614.64,
   "end": 616.88,
   "text": "these contaminants into the outside air.",
   "zh": "排放到室外空气中。"
  },
  {
   "start": 618.0,
   "end": 619.92,
   "text": "The most effective of these systems",
   "zh": "这些系统中最有效的"
  },
  {
   "start": 619.92,
   "end": 622.48,
   "text": "is the high-efficiency particulate air,",
   "zh": "是高效空气颗粒过滤器，"
  },
  {
   "start": 622.48,
   "end": 623.96,
   "text": "HEPA filter.",
   "zh": "即 HEPA 过滤器。"
  },
  {
   "start": 623.96,
   "end": 625.4,
   "text": "A HEPA filter captures",
   "zh": "HEPA 过滤器能捕获"
  },
  {
   "start": 625.4,
   "end": 626.64,
   "text": "particulates as small",
   "zh": "小至"
  },
  {
   "start": 626.64,
   "end": 628.48,
   "text": "as three-tenths of a micron",
   "zh": "0.3 微米的颗粒物，"
  },
  {
   "start": 628.48,
   "end": 632.36,
   "text": "at a success rate of 99.99%.",
   "zh": "捕获率达 99.99%。"
  },
  {
   "start": 632.36,
   "end": 633.28,
   "text": "Remember, though,",
   "zh": "不过要记住，"
  },
  {
   "start": 633.28,
   "end": 634.2,
   "text": "the HEPA filter",
   "zh": "HEPA 过滤器"
  },
  {
   "start": 634.2,
   "end": 635.96,
   "text": "is a particulate filter.",
   "zh": "是一种颗粒物过滤器。"
  },
  {
   "start": 635.96,
   "end": 638.2,
   "text": "It does not prevent hazardous gases",
   "zh": "它不能阻止有害气体"
  },
  {
   "start": 638.2,
   "end": 639.0,
   "text": "from passing through",
   "zh": "通过"
  },
  {
   "start": 639.0,
   "end": 640.88,
   "text": "the exhaust system.",
   "zh": "排风系统。"
  },
  {
   "start": 640.88,
   "end": 642.2,
   "text": "If the substances you're working",
   "zh": "如果你所使用的物质"
  },
  {
   "start": 642.2,
   "end": 643.84,
   "text": "with give off hazardous particles",
   "zh": "会散发出有害颗粒物"
  },
  {
   "start": 643.84,
   "end": 645.16,
   "text": "and gases,",
   "zh": "和气体，"
  },
  {
   "start": 645.16,
   "end": 646.48,
   "text": "talk to your supervisor",
   "zh": "就和你的主管谈一谈，"
  },
  {
   "start": 646.48,
   "end": 647.76,
   "text": "about which hoods in your lab",
   "zh": "了解实验室里哪些通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 647.76,
   "end": 652.02,
   "text": "will protect you from both hazards.",
   "zh": "能同时防护这两种危害。"
  },
  {
   "start": 652.02,
   "end": 653.18,
   "text": "There are hoods that provide",
   "zh": "还有一些通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 653.18,
   "end": 654.14,
   "text": "protection against",
   "zh": "能够防护"
  },
  {
   "start": 654.14,
   "end": 656.34,
   "text": "other specialized hazards as well.",
   "zh": "其他特殊危害。"
  },
  {
   "start": 656.34,
   "end": 658.1,
   "text": "While you may not normally use them,",
   "zh": "虽然你平时可能不会用到它们，"
  },
  {
   "start": 658.1,
   "end": 659.98,
   "text": "you should know what they are there for",
   "zh": "但你应该知道它们是做什么用的，"
  },
  {
   "start": 659.98,
   "end": 661.66,
   "text": "and how they work.",
   "zh": "以及它们是如何工作的。"
  },
  {
   "start": 661.66,
   "end": 662.94,
   "text": "The most common of these hoods",
   "zh": "这类通风柜中最常见的"
  },
  {
   "start": 662.94,
   "end": 664.62,
   "text": "are used with perchloric acids",
   "zh": "是用于高氯酸"
  },
  {
   "start": 664.62,
   "end": 666.3,
   "text": "and radioisotopes.",
   "zh": "和放射性同位素的。"
  },
  {
   "start": 667.54,
   "end": 668.94,
   "text": "The distinguishing feature",
   "zh": "高氯酸通风柜的"
  },
  {
   "start": 668.94,
   "end": 670.46,
   "text": "of a perchloric acid hood",
   "zh": "显著特点"
  },
  {
   "start": 670.46,
   "end": 672.46,
   "text": "is its washdown capability.",
   "zh": "是它具有冲洗功能。"
  },
  {
   "start": 672.46,
   "end": 674.06,
   "text": "This prevents the dangerous buildup",
   "zh": "这能防止反应性残留物"
  },
  {
   "start": 674.06,
   "end": 675.62,
   "text": "of reactive residues.",
   "zh": "危险地积聚。"
  },
  {
   "start": 676.7,
   "end": 677.86,
   "text": "One thing to remember,",
   "zh": "有一点要记住，"
  },
  {
   "start": 677.86,
   "end": 679.02,
   "text": "organic materials",
   "zh": "有机物"
  },
  {
   "start": 679.02,
   "end": 680.06,
   "text": "should never be used",
   "zh": "绝不应在"
  },
  {
   "start": 680.06,
   "end": 682.26,
   "text": "in perchloric acid hoods.",
   "zh": "高氯酸通风柜中使用。"
  },
  {
   "start": 682.26,
   "end": 683.66,
   "text": "An explosive reaction",
   "zh": "有机物与酸的残留物混合"
  },
  {
   "start": 683.66,
   "end": 685.3,
   "text": "may result from the mixture",
   "zh": "可能会"
  },
  {
   "start": 685.3,
   "end": 689.51,
   "text": "of organics and the acids residue.",
   "zh": "引发爆炸性反应。"
  },
  {
   "start": 689.51,
   "end": 690.95,
   "text": "If you're working with material",
   "zh": "如果你处理的物质"
  },
  {
   "start": 690.95,
   "end": 692.11,
   "text": "that is radioactive,",
   "zh": "具有放射性，"
  },
  {
   "start": 692.11,
   "end": 693.07,
   "text": "you should be using",
   "zh": "你就应该使用"
  },
  {
   "start": 693.07,
   "end": 695.03,
   "text": "a radioisotope hood.",
   "zh": "放射性同位素通风柜。"
  },
  {
   "start": 695.03,
   "end": 696.43,
   "text": "This hood is impermeable",
   "zh": "这种通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 696.43,
   "end": 697.95,
   "text": "to radioactive material",
   "zh": "不会被放射性物质渗透，"
  },
  {
   "start": 697.95,
   "end": 713.63,
   "text": "and will minimize dangerous exposure.",
   "zh": "能最大限度地减少危险暴露。"
  },
  {
   "start": 713.63,
   "end": 714.95,
   "text": "No matter what type of hood",
   "zh": "无论你使用的是"
  },
  {
   "start": 714.95,
   "end": 715.59,
   "text": "you're using",
   "zh": "哪种类型的通风柜，"
  },
  {
   "start": 715.59,
   "end": 717.39,
   "text": "or how many precautions you take,",
   "zh": "或者采取了多少预防措施，"
  },
  {
   "start": 717.39,
   "end": 719.59,
   "text": "things can still go wrong.",
   "zh": "事情仍然可能出错。"
  },
  {
   "start": 719.59,
   "end": 721.51,
   "text": "So it's important to be prepared",
   "zh": "所以做好准备很重要，"
  },
  {
   "start": 721.51,
   "end": 723.63,
   "text": "in the event a hood-related accident",
   "zh": "以防实验室里发生"
  },
  {
   "start": 723.63,
   "end": 725.11,
   "text": "occurs in your lab.",
   "zh": "与通风柜有关的事故。"
  },
  {
   "start": 726.55,
   "end": 728.03,
   "text": "Spills inside a hood",
   "zh": "通风柜内的溅洒"
  },
  {
   "start": 728.03,
   "end": 730.27,
   "text": "need to be dealt with immediately.",
   "zh": "需要立即处理。"
  },
  {
   "start": 730.27,
   "end": 731.35,
   "text": "Follow your facility's",
   "zh": "遵守你们设施的"
  },
  {
   "start": 731.35,
   "end": 732.87,
   "text": "cleanup procedures.",
   "zh": "清理程序。"
  },
  {
   "start": 732.87,
   "end": 733.91,
   "text": "Soak up the spill",
   "zh": "用吸附材料"
  },
  {
   "start": 733.91,
   "end": 735.27,
   "text": "with an absorbent material",
   "zh": "吸干溅洒物，"
  },
  {
   "start": 735.27,
   "end": 736.95,
   "text": "and dispose of it properly.",
   "zh": "并妥善处置。"
  },
  {
   "start": 738.43,
   "end": 740.51,
   "text": "Before handling any substance,",
   "zh": "在处理任何物质之前，"
  },
  {
   "start": 740.51,
   "end": 743.03,
   "text": "you should read its safety data sheet.",
   "zh": "你都应该阅读它的安全技术说明书。"
  },
  {
   "start": 743.03,
   "end": 744.71,
   "text": "Effective emergency response",
   "zh": "有效的应急响应"
  },
  {
   "start": 744.71,
   "end": 745.99,
   "text": "begins with your knowledge",
   "zh": "始于你对"
  },
  {
   "start": 745.99,
   "end": 747.43,
   "text": "of the spilled material.",
   "zh": "溅洒物质的了解。"
  },
  {
   "start": 748.51,
   "end": 750.07,
   "text": "Small fires in a hood",
   "zh": "通风柜内的小火"
  },
  {
   "start": 750.07,
   "end": 750.83,
   "text": "can be put out",
   "zh": "可以用"
  },
  {
   "start": 750.83,
   "end": 751.83,
   "text": "with extinguishers",
   "zh": "灭火器扑灭，"
  },
  {
   "start": 751.83,
   "end": 753.35,
   "text": "or through suffocation",
   "zh": "或者通过窒息法，"
  },
  {
   "start": 753.35,
   "end": 754.19,
   "text": "by covering them",
   "zh": "用表面皿"
  },
  {
   "start": 754.19,
   "end": 755.15,
   "text": "with a watch glass",
   "zh": "或倒扣的烧杯"
  },
  {
   "start": 755.15,
   "end": 756.87,
   "text": "or inverted beaker.",
   "zh": "把它盖住。"
  },
  {
   "start": 756.87,
   "end": 757.91,
   "text": "Some hoods even have",
   "zh": "有些通风柜甚至有"
  },
  {
   "start": 757.91,
   "end": 760.27,
   "text": "their own fire suppression systems.",
   "zh": "自带的灭火系统。"
  },
  {
   "start": 760.27,
   "end": 761.71,
   "text": "With them, all you have to do",
   "zh": "有了它们，你只需"
  },
  {
   "start": 761.71,
   "end": 762.91,
   "text": "is flick a switch.",
   "zh": "拨一下开关。"
  },
  {
   "start": 764.11,
   "end": 765.07,
   "text": "But in any case,",
   "zh": "但无论如何，"
  },
  {
   "start": 765.07,
   "end": 766.03,
   "text": "you should know where",
   "zh": "你都应该知道"
  },
  {
   "start": 766.03,
   "end": 767.39,
   "text": "the nearest fire extinguisher",
   "zh": "实验室里最近的灭火器"
  },
  {
   "start": 767.39,
   "end": 770.91,
   "text": "is in your lab.",
   "zh": "在哪里。"
  },
  {
   "start": 770.91,
   "end": 771.71,
   "text": "In the event of",
   "zh": "如果发生"
  },
  {
   "start": 771.71,
   "end": 773.43,
   "text": "an uncontrollable fire,",
   "zh": "无法控制的火灾，"
  },
  {
   "start": 773.43,
   "end": 775.51,
   "text": "close the sash and get out.",
   "zh": "就关上柜门并撤离。"
  },
  {
   "start": 775.51,
   "end": 776.43,
   "text": "Sound the alarm",
   "zh": "拉响警报，"
  },
  {
   "start": 776.43,
   "end": 780.87,
   "text": "and call the fire department.",
   "zh": "并打电话给消防部门。"
  },
  {
   "start": 780.87,
   "end": 782.15,
   "text": "Ventilation failures",
   "zh": "通风故障"
  },
  {
   "start": 782.15,
   "end": 783.67,
   "text": "are another type of emergency",
   "zh": "是另一类"
  },
  {
   "start": 783.67,
   "end": 785.63,
   "text": "that you should be prepared for.",
   "zh": "你应该做好准备的紧急情况。"
  },
  {
   "start": 785.63,
   "end": 786.51,
   "text": "A motor failure",
   "zh": "电机故障"
  },
  {
   "start": 786.51,
   "end": 787.39,
   "text": "or malfunction",
   "zh": "或电线"
  },
  {
   "start": 787.39,
   "end": 788.39,
   "text": "in the electrical lines",
   "zh": "出现故障，"
  },
  {
   "start": 788.39,
   "end": 789.23,
   "text": "can bring your hood's",
   "zh": "都可能使通风柜的"
  },
  {
   "start": 789.23,
   "end": 790.23,
   "text": "ventilation system",
   "zh": "通风系统"
  },
  {
   "start": 790.23,
   "end": 791.59,
   "text": "to a standstill,",
   "zh": "停止运转，"
  },
  {
   "start": 791.59,
   "end": 793.15,
   "text": "releasing harmful fumes,",
   "zh": "在此过程中"
  },
  {
   "start": 793.15,
   "end": 794.55,
   "text": "vapors and particles",
   "zh": "释放出有害的烟气、"
  },
  {
   "start": 794.55,
   "end": 796.75,
   "text": "in the process.",
   "zh": "蒸气和颗粒。"
  },
  {
   "start": 796.75,
   "end": 798.07,
   "text": "Talk to your supervisor",
   "zh": "和你的主管谈一谈"
  },
  {
   "start": 798.07,
   "end": 799.27,
   "text": "about your facility's",
   "zh": "你们设施的"
  },
  {
   "start": 799.27,
   "end": 800.51,
   "text": "emergency plan",
   "zh": "应急预案，"
  },
  {
   "start": 800.51,
   "end": 801.83,
   "text": "so that you'll know exactly",
   "zh": "这样你就能确切地知道"
  },
  {
   "start": 801.83,
   "end": 802.75,
   "text": "what to do in case",
   "zh": "在发生"
  },
  {
   "start": 802.75,
   "end": 803.91,
   "text": "of an equipment failure",
   "zh": "设备故障"
  },
  {
   "start": 803.91,
   "end": 812.1,
   "text": "or other ventilation problem.",
   "zh": "或其他通风问题时该怎么做。"
  },
  {
   "start": 812.1,
   "end": 813.86,
   "text": "You can never be too careful",
   "zh": "使用实验室通风柜时，"
  },
  {
   "start": 813.86,
   "end": 815.7,
   "text": "when using a laboratory hood.",
   "zh": "再怎么小心都不为过。"
  },
  {
   "start": 815.7,
   "end": 816.94,
   "text": "Remember, the reason",
   "zh": "记住，你之所以"
  },
  {
   "start": 816.94,
   "end": 818.22,
   "text": "you're working under a hood",
   "zh": "在通风柜里操作，"
  },
  {
   "start": 818.22,
   "end": 819.22,
   "text": "is that you're handling",
   "zh": "是因为你正在处理"
  },
  {
   "start": 819.22,
   "end": 821.98,
   "text": "substances that are hazardous.",
   "zh": "有害的物质。"
  },
  {
   "start": 821.98,
   "end": 825.39,
   "text": "Let's review.",
   "zh": "我们来回顾一下。"
  },
  {
   "start": 825.39,
   "end": 826.19,
   "text": "Make sure the hoods",
   "zh": "确保你所使用的"
  },
  {
   "start": 826.19,
   "end": 826.83,
   "text": "you work with",
   "zh": "通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 826.83,
   "end": 828.03,
   "text": "are set up correctly",
   "zh": "设置正确，"
  },
  {
   "start": 828.03,
   "end": 828.95,
   "text": "and that they meet",
   "zh": "并且满足"
  },
  {
   "start": 828.95,
   "end": 832.31,
   "text": "all performance requirements.",
   "zh": "所有性能要求。"
  },
  {
   "start": 832.31,
   "end": 833.31,
   "text": "Keep all of your work",
   "zh": "让你所有的操作"
  },
  {
   "start": 833.31,
   "end": 834.63,
   "text": "at least six inches",
   "zh": "都在通风柜内"
  },
  {
   "start": 834.63,
   "end": 837.86,
   "text": "inside the hood.",
   "zh": "至少六英寸处进行。"
  },
  {
   "start": 837.86,
   "end": 838.9,
   "text": "Don't use your hood",
   "zh": "不要把你的通风柜"
  },
  {
   "start": 838.9,
   "end": 840.38,
   "text": "as a storage cabinet.",
   "zh": "当作储物柜。"
  },
  {
   "start": 840.38,
   "end": 841.98,
   "text": "Too many objects inside a hood",
   "zh": "通风柜里的东西太多"
  },
  {
   "start": 841.98,
   "end": 845.82,
   "text": "can distort its airflow.",
   "zh": "会扰乱它的气流。"
  },
  {
   "start": 845.82,
   "end": 846.5,
   "text": "Pay attention",
   "zh": "留意"
  },
  {
   "start": 846.5,
   "end": 847.82,
   "text": "to your airflow monitors",
   "zh": "你的气流监测器，"
  },
  {
   "start": 847.82,
   "end": 849.38,
   "text": "and keep the hood sashed down",
   "zh": "操作时"
  },
  {
   "start": 849.38,
   "end": 850.42,
   "text": "as far as possible",
   "zh": "尽量把柜门"
  },
  {
   "start": 850.42,
   "end": 852.98,
   "text": "when you work.",
   "zh": "往下拉。"
  },
  {
   "start": 852.98,
   "end": 854.46,
   "text": "Be sure your hood is checked",
   "zh": "确保你的通风柜定期接受检查"
  },
  {
   "start": 854.46,
   "end": 858.02,
   "text": "or recertified regularly.",
   "zh": "或重新认证。"
  },
  {
   "start": 858.02,
   "end": 859.3,
   "text": "And be prepared in case",
   "zh": "并做好准备，以防"
  },
  {
   "start": 859.3,
   "end": 864.21,
   "text": "of a hood-related emergency.",
   "zh": "发生与通风柜有关的紧急情况。"
  },
  {
   "start": 864.21,
   "end": 865.49,
   "text": "Choosing the right hood",
   "zh": "为工作选择合适的"
  },
  {
   "start": 865.49,
   "end": 866.25,
   "text": "for the job",
   "zh": "通风柜，"
  },
  {
   "start": 866.25,
   "end": 867.89,
   "text": "and working with it correctly",
   "zh": "并正确地使用它，"
  },
  {
   "start": 867.89,
   "end": 869.45,
   "text": "will isolate the contaminants",
   "zh": "就能隔离你的工作"
  },
  {
   "start": 869.45,
   "end": 870.81,
   "text": "your work may generate",
   "zh": "可能产生的污染物，"
  },
  {
   "start": 870.81,
   "end": 871.81,
   "text": "and keep you",
   "zh": "保障你"
  },
  {
   "start": 871.81,
   "end": 874.45,
   "text": "and your coworkers safe.",
   "zh": "和你的同事的安全。"
  }
 ]
}